1
00:00:00,400 --> 00:00:02,243
So… you summarised your agent's

2
00:00:02,293 --> 00:00:04,505
<font color="#00FFFF"><b>conversation history</b></font> hoping it'd save money.

3
00:00:04,555 --> 00:00:06,155
And your bill just <font color="#FF5252"><b>tripled</b></font>.

4
00:00:06,205 --> 00:00:08,785
Here's the thing — APIs are <font color="#00FFFF"><b>stateless</b></font>.

5
00:00:08,835 --> 00:00:10,309
The model doesn't remember.

6
00:00:10,359 --> 00:00:12,571
You send your entire <font color="#00FFFF"><b>conversation history</b></font>

7
00:00:12,621 --> 00:00:14,096
in every single request.

8
00:00:14,146 --> 00:00:15,251
Compounding every turn.

9
00:00:15,301 --> 00:00:18,250
So twenty messages, a thousand tokens each —

10
00:00:18,300 --> 00:00:20,512
you didn't send twenty thousand tokens.

11
00:00:20,562 --> 00:00:22,062
You sent <font color="#FF5252"><b>two hundred and ten thousand</b></font>.

12
00:00:22,112 --> 00:00:25,061
And the only reason that doesn't bankrupt you

13
00:00:25,111 --> 00:00:28,797
is that most of it is identical to last time,

14
00:00:28,847 --> 00:00:31,059
so it comes back from <font color="#00FFFF"><b>cache</b></font>

15
00:00:31,109 --> 00:00:33,689
at about a tenth of the price.

16
00:00:33,739 --> 00:00:37,057
<font color="#FFD700"><b>One:</b></font> your bill isn't the length of the conversation.

17
00:00:37,107 --> 00:00:38,507
It's how much of it you're <font color="#FFD700"><b>recomputing</b></font>.

18
00:00:38,557 --> 00:00:40,400
Now your conversation gets bigger.

19
00:00:40,450 --> 00:00:43,030
So you do the obvious thing —

20
00:00:43,080 --> 00:00:44,923
you keep a <font color="#00FFFF"><b>running summary</b></font>.

21
00:00:44,973 --> 00:00:47,922
Every turn, you squash the old history down

22
00:00:47,972 --> 00:00:49,446
to keep it small.

23
00:00:49,496 --> 00:00:51,096
And that's the <font color="#FF5252"><b>trap</b></font>.

24
00:00:51,146 --> 00:00:53,358
Because each turn, the summary absorbs

25
00:00:53,408 --> 00:00:54,514
one more message.

26
00:00:54,564 --> 00:00:56,776
So it's different text every time.

27
00:00:56,826 --> 00:00:58,669
Different text, different <font color="#00FFFF"><b>prefix</b></font> —

28
00:00:58,719 --> 00:01:01,299
and a different prefix is a <font color="#FF5252"><b>miss</b></font>.

29
00:01:01,349 --> 00:01:03,929
So you <font color="#FF5252"><b>never get a hit</b></font>. Ever.

30
00:01:03,979 --> 00:01:07,665
Those turns were costing you a tenth of the price,

31
00:01:07,715 --> 00:01:11,401
and now you're paying <font color="#FF5252"><b>more than full price</b></font> for them,

32
00:01:11,451 --> 00:01:12,926
on every single request.

33
00:01:12,976 --> 00:01:15,556
<font color="#FFD700"><b>Two:</b></font> it's not compression that costs you.

34
00:01:15,606 --> 00:01:16,343
It's <font color="#FF5252"><b>re-compression</b></font>.

35
00:01:16,393 --> 00:01:17,793
Half the tokens, <font color="#FF5252"><b>three times the bill</b></font>.

36
00:01:17,843 --> 00:01:19,143
So don't rewrite. <font color="#FFD700"><b>Append</b></font>.

37
00:01:19,193 --> 00:01:22,511
Everything that never changes goes at the front —

38
00:01:22,561 --> 00:01:25,141
your <font color="#00FFFF"><b>tools</b></font>, your <font color="#00FFFF"><b>system prompt</b></font>, your <font color="#00FFFF"><b>documents</b></font>.

39
00:01:25,191 --> 00:01:26,297
Then the history.

40
00:01:26,347 --> 00:01:28,190
Then the new message, last.

41
00:01:28,240 --> 00:01:30,452
And your cache <font color="#00FFFF"><b>breakpoint</b></font> goes on

42
00:01:30,502 --> 00:01:32,714
the last thing that doesn't move.

43
00:01:32,764 --> 00:01:34,607
You grow to the right.

44
00:01:34,657 --> 00:01:36,500
You never touch the left.

45
00:01:36,550 --> 00:01:39,130
And when the window genuinely fills up,

46
00:01:39,180 --> 00:01:40,654
you <font color="#FFD700"><b>compact once</b></font> —

47
00:01:40,704 --> 00:01:42,916
that summary becomes your new <font color="#00FFFF"><b>prefix</b></font>,

48
00:01:42,966 --> 00:01:45,178
and it caches from there on.

49
00:01:45,228 --> 00:01:45,965
Same technique.

50
00:01:46,015 --> 00:01:48,227
It's the frequency that changes everything.

51
00:01:48,277 --> 00:01:49,751
<font color="#FFD700"><b>Three:</b></font> compact at <font color="#FFD700"><b>boundaries</b></font>,

52
00:01:49,801 --> 00:01:51,101
never <font color="#FF5252"><b>mid-flight</b></font>.

53
00:01:51,151 --> 00:01:54,100
Full arithmetic's in the <font color="#FFD700"><b>vault</b></font>, <font color="#FFD700"><b>link in bio</b></font>.

54
00:01:54,150 --> 00:01:55,550
<font color="#FFD700"><b>Follow along for the series</b></font>.
